# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored, read automatically by vite) to point a LOCAL dev server at
# a specific module. You do NOT need this file to work on the pages: with nothing set, the page
# derives the module from its own host (`http://<the host you loaded from>:3000`) and uses the
# `fairdrop-scratch` database — which is correct whenever `spacetime start` is running on the
# same machine serving the page, including from a phone on the same wifi.
#
# Set these when the module is somewhere else. The DEPLOYED build gets the same two variables
# from `vercel.json`, so this file is only ever about local development.
#
# Only `VITE_`-prefixed variables reach the browser. That is vite's rule, not ours, and it is
# why these are named this way.

# Must be https:// for any deployed page — an HTTPS page cannot open a plaintext ws://, and the
# SDK derives its socket scheme from this value.
VITE_STDB_URI=https://maincloud.spacetimedb.com

# Never `fairdrop-scratch` when pointing at a shared module: scratch is the throwaway.
VITE_STDB_DB=fairdrop-demo
